## 1. Whole-tree per-file census, both precisions, both trees

Occurrences (`unwrap()` counts every match):

    D=$H/reference/rust/gen     # then $F/.../rust/gen and both rust-f32
    find "$D" -type f -name '*.rs' -print0 | xargs -0 grep -ho -- 'unwrap()' | wc -l
    find "$D" -type f -name '*.rs' -print0 | xargs -0 grep -ho -- 'Result<'  | wc -l

Lines (`grep -c` semantics, one per matching line per file):

    find "$D" -type f -name '*.rs' -print0 \
      | xargs -0 grep -hc -- 'unwrap()' | awk '{s+=$1} END{print s+0}'

Per-file TSVs: for each `*.rs` under `reference/<prec>/gen`, append
`<count>\t<path-relative-to-gen>`.

    while IFS= read -r f; do
      rel="${f#$d/}"
      printf '%s\t%s\n' "$(grep -o -- 'unwrap()' "$f" | wc -l)" "$rel"
      printf '%s\t%s\n' "$(grep -o -- 'Result<'  "$f" | wc -l)" "$rel"
    done < <(find "$d" -type f -name '*.rs' | sort)

Per-file deltas:

